            "labels": [
 
            ],
            "state": "open",
            "assignee": null,
            "milestone": null,
            "comments": 2,
            "created_at": "2013-10-10T08:59:59Z",
            "updated_at": "2013-10-11T20:09:00Z",
            "closed_at": null,
            "pull_request": {
                "html_url": null,
                "diff_url": null,
                "patch_url": null
            },
            "body": "I finalized the EJS templates plugin for CanJS with templates pre-compilation support. Sources are example are available here: https://github.com/isadovskiy/canjs-require-ejs\r\n\r\nThere are few configuration tricks, which should be done in config.js and build.js in order to make everything works. I will explain them later in readme. CanJS library sources are also tweaked a little bit to eliminate direct dependencies from window and document in the source files, which are required for EJS templates compilation.\r\n\r\nCanJS team, if you are interesting in integration this solution into your framework, I can provide all necessary information and support."
        },
        "comment": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitovi/canjs/issues/comments/26168223",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/bitovi/canjs/issues/491#issuecomment-26168223",
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitovi/canjs/issues/491",
            "id": 26168223,
            "user": {
                "login": "isadovskiy",
                "id": 3382990,
                "avatar_url": "https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/5416f20dc11e5b58286ebb3c8dd4a85f?d=https%3A%2F%2Fidenticons.github.com%2F23e2e6738ea7ef3483f17d975b3dd3e3.png",
                "gravatar_id": "5416f20dc11e5b58286ebb3c8dd4a85f",
                "url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy",
                "html_url": "https://github.com/isadovskiy",
                "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/followers",
                "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/following{/other_user}",
                "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/gists{/gist_id}",
                "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
                "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/subscriptions",
                "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/orgs",
                "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/repos",
                "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/events{/privacy}",
                "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/isadovskiy/received_events",
                "type": "User",
                "site_admin": false
            },
            "created_at": "2013-10-11T20:09:00Z",
            "updated_at": "2013-10-11T20:09:00Z",
            "body": "In general yes.\r\n\r\nBut the main trick is here: https://github.com/isadovskiy/canjs-require-ejs/blob/master/src/plugin/ejs.builder.js:\r\n\r\n require.config({\r\n     map: {\r\n         '*': {\r\n             'can/util/library': 'can/util/optimize'\r\n         }\r\n     }\r\n });\r\n\r\nIt replaces core library, which has DOM dependencies with my own, which provide few DOM-independent routines, required for EJS compilation. Since it's replaced in plugin builder, it affects just executions in optimizer environment.\r\n\r\nCurrently \"can/util/optimize\" is mapped to ejs.library in build.js:\r\n\r\n    paths: {\r\n        'can/util/optimize': 'plugin/ejs.library'\r\n    }\r\n\r\nBut in general can/util/optimize should be a part of the CanJS and named \"can/util/core\" or something similar. And should replace \"can/util/library\" with map config to run plugins in optimizer environment."
        }
    },
